# box-mounts — EXTRA paths the agent boxes see, on top of their checkout. Edit from the hub with
# `cbx expose` / `cbx hide`, or by hand. All sources are confined under the golden tree by the
# broker. Recreate a box (cbx recreate <box>) to apply changes.
#
# The checkout itself is NOT configured here any more: every box gets an overlayfs view of the
# shared prepared golden tree (data/golden/current) at /home/dev/repo, writing into its own
# upper layer. That's what makes N agents cost N x (their own diff) instead of N full checkouts,
# and it's why each box has a real .git and works on its own branch (agent/<box>).
#
# Grammar (whitespace-separated; '#'/blank ignored):
#   TREE <dst> <ro|rw>     where the overlay checkout lands (default: 'repo rw'). 'ro' mounts the
#                          golden directly read-only instead — no upper layer, no writes, no git
#                          bootstrap. Useful for a look-but-don't-touch box.
#   <src> <dst> <ro|rw>    golden/<src> bind-mounted at /home/dev/<dst>
#
# Default (this file absent or empty): just the overlay checkout at /home/dev/repo. That is the
# normal setup — you only need lines here for something outside the repo tree.

# Examples:

# Put the checkout somewhere else in the box's home
#   TREE work rw

# A read-only box that can look at the code but never change it
#   TREE repo ro

# Additionally expose a subdirectory read-only at a second path (e.g. reference material)
#   docs  reference  ro
